      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Psychological_pricing english page, has a japanese page linked:\n\nhttps://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%82%A4%E3%83%81%E3%82%AD%E3%83%A5%E3%83%83%E3%83%91  \"イチキュッパ\"\n\nI think the current pricing structure is fine. If they were to adjust things, however it's done,  we'd be paying more for the lower amounts. They can try and hide it by showing buyers bonus credits, and giving sellers lower amounts when they pull money out, but then the sellers likely will raise prices...\n\nI'm used to the .99 thing, so they write $4.99 and I see $5. I think if I need $20 in vbucks, I'm going to be okay with eating 3 cents to save some time.",
